  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Monday 15 May 1939. There was no contest; the political representation stayed at seven Nationalists, four Unionists and one Independent (Belfast News-Letter, 6 May 1939, p. 9). No contest in the South Ward. Returned unopposed."
